orious for having  high-end property that's purchased by  the rich and famous for example rapper  50 cent recently sold his Connecticut  mansion for 2.9 million dollars in  Beetlejuice director Tim Burton pokes  fun at the wealthy invaders from out of  state who blessed her into a sleepy town  and drive up the property value this  type of reference requires a working  knowledge of social politics and real  estate anxieties in order to really  appreciate it something that most young  viewers won't readily understand  perfectly portrayed by Michael Keaton  the character of Beetlejuice is a lot in  every sense of the word he's loud he's  brash he's completely over the top most  of the things he says in his used car  salesman patter  requires some solid pop-culture  background he claims that the Exorcist  keeps getting funnier every time he sees  it but hopefully young viewers haven't  seen that movie yet he also shouts go  ahead make my millennium and a clear  reference to the Dirty Harry movie set  an impact another film that most kids  probably wouldn't be too familiar with  and of course throughout the entire  movie Beetlejuice is a completely  unapologetic perv excuse me he's the  kind of ghost you definitely don't want  hanging around your teenage daughter or  your teenage son for that matter this is  played for laughs but adult viewers will  be creeped out by his treatment of Lydia  forcing her into a marriage and  reference  his intentions for their wedding night  basically Beetlejuice is the least  kid-friendly part of beetlejuice though  the name beetlejuice sounds  appropriately sinister for the movie's  main man it's also the name of a star in  the constellation Orion some  translations of the name which comes  from Arabic indicate that it means  armpit of Orion which kind of makes  sense for a guy with such questionable  personal hygiene otherwise the use of a  star's name and the actual sound of it  lends to a kind of mystical magical  witchy element to a 